WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.390
A bus stop.

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.630
Two strangers start chatting.

3
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.370
One steps closer.

4
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.400
The other edges back.

5
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.660
Closer.

6
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:09.590
Back.

7
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.470
Until they've shuffled
halfway along the pavement.

8
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.870
Somewhere else, two people chat
happily, much closer together.

9
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.550
Nobody steps back.

10
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.630
So who decided what the right gap is?

11
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.750
In this mission, you'll explore
how we send messages without words,

12
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.480
through eye contact, body
language and personal space.

13
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.880
You'll map the invisible zones around you,

14
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.350
from intimate, closest in, out to public.

15
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.480
And you'll ask whether the comfortable
distance is the same for everyone.

16
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:45.320
Your mission: work out who, or what,
sets the gap between you and a stranger.
